      "text": "The midline can also mean the average, so $\\left(\\frac{10+a+b+ab}{4}, 10, \\frac{10+a+b+ab}{4}\\right)$, the midpoint between 10 and $\\frac{10+a+b+ab}{4}$ means $10+\\frac{a+b+ab}{4}$, which is 10 only when $a+b+ab=0$, then when $A_{1}$ is true, $a + b + ab = 0$, this shares common roots, subtract A2: $a^2 + b^2 + ab + a + b = 0$, therefore when $a = 0$, $b^2 + b = 0$, when $a = -b$, $1 + b = 0$, the second case is impossible, this means that $a^2 + b^2$ and the first order are the same, so b can either be 0 or -1, then when $b = 0$, $a^2 + a = 0$, when $b = -1$, $1 + a = 0$, both cases are true. The number of solutions is 2.",
