      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given $10, a, b, ab$ is an arithmetic progression, we can write $a-b=ab-10$ and $b-a=ab-10a-10$.\n\nSquaring the first equation and resolving, we get $a^2=\\frac{300+90b}{b-10}$ and $b^2=\\frac{300+90a}{a-10}$.\n\nWe also have $ba-a^2=\\frac{2b+90}{b-10}$ and $ba-b^2=\\frac{2a+90}{a-10}$.\n\nMultiplying both sides of the third equation by $b-10$; $b^2b-10ba=b^2+90b$ and $ab^2-10ab=b^2+90a$.\n\nFinally we add up the first two equations to obtain $a^2+b^2-10b-10a=2b+90$.\n\nBy the arithmetic of the odds, this implies $\\frac{5}{7}$ must be even. Therefore, $\\boxed{0}$ pairs $(a,b)$ satisfy the given condition.",
